# Microservices Architecture & Frontend Restoration

This plan addresses your request to split the backend into two separate microservices and restore the missing frontend tracking/map functionality.

## Background Context
Currently, the `backend` handles everything in one process:
1. Scraping live data from UPSRTC/Margdarshi.
2. Calculating route geometries and learning new stops.
3. Serving frontend user searches (REST API) and WebSockets.

As you correctly observed, the heavy background engines can block the Node.js event loop, preventing the API from responding quickly to user searches.

## Proposed Architecture (Microservices)

We will split `apps/backend` into two distinct apps:

### 1. `apps/engine` (The Background Worker)
- **Role:** Purely for data ingestion and background processing.
- **Tasks:** Runs `adapter_live.ts` (polling UPSRTC) and `routeSeeder.ts` (learning new routes).
- **Communication:** Writes live data directly to the PostgreSQL database. Does not expose any HTTP ports.

### 2. `apps/backend` (The User API)
- **Role:** Purely for serving the frontend `web-app` and `admin` app.
- **Tasks:** Serves REST API (`/api/v1/journey`, `/stops`, etc.) and the WebSocket server for real-time tracking.
- **Communication:** Reads from PostgreSQL and broadcasts live updates. Will be 100% dedicated to user traffic, ensuring lightning-fast search responses.

## Proposed Changes

### Microservice Split
- [NEW] Create `apps/engine` directory with its own `package.json` and `tsconfig.json`.
- [MODIFY] Move `ingestion/` and `engine/routeSeeder.ts` logic into `apps/engine`.
- [MODIFY] Update `apps/backend/src/index.ts` to remove the background polling engines.
- [MODIFY] Update the root `package.json` and `turbo.json` to include the new `engine` app so that `npm run dev` starts all 3 services (`web-app`, `backend`, `engine`).

